# Kabyle night. Attested by native speaker athmanemokraoui (#265).
# Boundaries fall back to chronologia's default night convention.
iḍ
iḍ-a
# Dallet, Dictionnaire kabyle-français (SELAF 1982) p. 170: "iḍ (yi),
# pl. uḍan / aḍan (wa) / iḍan (yi), Nuit".  Dallet marks iḍan "peu employé",
# and iḍan is also the plural of "dog", so it is not listed.
uḍan
aḍan
# Dallet, Dictionnaire français-kabyle (SELAF 1985) p. 168: "Nuit : iḍ Ḍ 170.
# llil L 442".
llil
# Native answer, chronologia#1489 (comment 7218700864): "n yiḍ" or "n deg yiḍ" (at night).
n yiḍ
n deg yiḍ
